{"name":"Rhodes","hex":"#89c0e6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Rhodes","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An island of the Dodecanese, Greece in the Aegean Sea.","A city on the island of Rhodes, Greece, and the capital of the Dodecanese."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A topographic surname for a person who lived near woodland clearings, or a habitational one for someone from a place so named.","A male given name transferred from the surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Rhodes"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rhodes","blocks":[{"text":"Rhodes is the largest of Greece's Dodecanese islands and their historical capital, as well as the ninth largest island in the Mediterranean Sea. Administratively, Rhodes constitutes a municipality within the Rhodes regional unit, which is part of the South Aegean administrative region. The principal town of the island and seat of the municipality is the city of Rhodes, home to 50,636 inhabitants according to the 2011 census. By 2022, the island's population had grown to 125,113 people. Located northeast of Crete and southeast of Athens, Rhodes is referred to by several nicknames: \"the Island of the Sun\" after its patron sun god Helios; \"the Pearl Island\"; and \"the Island of the Knights\", a reference to the Knights of Saint John of Jerusalem, who ruled the island from 1310 to 1522."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Rhodes_sentinel2_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Rhodes_sentinel2_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhodes"},{"title":"Rhodes (city)","blocks":[{"text":"Rhodes is the principal city and a former municipality on the island of Rhodes in the Dodecanese, Greece. Since the 2011 local government reform, it is part of the municipality Rhodes, of which it is the seat and a municipal unit. It has a population of approximately 56,000 with nearly 90,000 in its metropolitan area. Rhodes has been famous since antiquity as the site of Colossus of Rhodes, one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World. The citadel of Rhodes, built by the Hospitallers, is one of the best-preserved medieval towns in Europe. The Medieval city is designated as a UNESCO World Heritage Site."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Medieval_City_of_Rhodes_03.jpg/330px-Medieval_City_of_Rhodes_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhodes_(city)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/2011_Dimos_Rodou.png/500px-2011_Dimos_Rodou.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/2011_Dimos_Rodou.png/1280px-2011_Dimos_Rodou.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/2011_Dimos_Rodou.png/500px-2011_Dimos_Rodou.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2011_Dimos_Rodou.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Lindos_Rhodes_1.jpg/500px-Lindos_Rhodes_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Lindos_Rhodes_1.jpg/1280px-Lindos_Rhodes_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Lindos_Rhodes_1.jpg/500px-Lindos_Rhodes_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"General view of the village of Lindos, with the acropolis and beaches, island of Rhodes, Greece","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALindos_Rhodes_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu